{
 "id": "2022-juanga-davao",
 "name": "Davao City Dual Roadways: Contemplative Landscape Rating (1–6)",
 "description": "Method replication: participants rate dual roadways in Davao City, each shown from two viewpoints side by side, on the seven features of the Contemplative Landscape Model (landscape layers, landform, vegetation, colour and light, compatibility, archetypal elements, character of peace and silence) from 1 (lowest) to 6 (highest). The images are not the paper's stimuli (Google Street View panoramas of Roxas Avenue, Quirino Avenue and Dacudao Avenue fetched for this template, 2022–2026 captures).\n\nOriginal study: Juanga & Delos Reyes (2022), \"Introspective Visual Quality Assessment of Dual Thoroughfare Streetscapes in Davao City\", Environment and Urbanization ASIA 13(2), 232–246. Davao City residents in two age groups (18–38 and 39–60; 75 participants reported) rated five dual roadways with median strips, each shown in two Google Street View images, in an online Google Forms survey adapted from the Contemplative Landscape Questionnaire; Roxas Avenue scored highest (mean 4.44) and Manambulan-Tagakpan Road lowest (4.07).\n\nDifferences from the original study: (1) three of the five streets; C.P. Garcia Highway and Manambulan-Tagakpan Road are left out because a section with a landscaped median could not be located in current Street View, and researchers can add their own street images to the \"davao\" folder; (2) new viewpoints, not the paper's images; (3) a short description of each feature is shown, written for this template rather than taken from the paper's adapted questionnaire.",
